# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SoftAura Technology — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for development. `.env.local` is gitignored; never commit
# real credentials. Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are exposed to the browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Canonical site origin. Used for metadata, Open Graph URLs, sitemap and robots.
# No trailing slash. Set this per environment — the code falls back to the
# production domain, which would emit wrong absolute URLs on a preview deploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Google Analytics 4 measurement ID.
# Optional. The code falls back to the production property, so a deploy that
# omits this still reports. Set it to a *different* ID to point a staging or
# preview environment at its own property, or to an empty value to switch
# analytics off entirely for that environment.
# Not a secret — it is served to every visitor in the page source.
# Analytics never loads in development regardless of this value; to check it
# locally, run `npm run build && npm start`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-HX19V58CGE

# Scheduling link for the booking card on /contact — Cal.com, Calendly or similar.
# Optional. Unset, <BookingEmbed> falls back to the phone numbers and WhatsApp
# links instead of rendering an empty widget (see src/components/BookingEmbed.tsx).
NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_URL=

# --- Enquiry delivery ------------------------------------------------------
#
# The contact form needs ONE of the two transports below. With neither set, a
# production deployment returns an error to the visitor and tells them to email
# directly — it does NOT claim the message was sent. Development is the
# exception: with nothing configured, enquiries are logged to the console and
# reported as successful, so the form can be worked on without secrets.
#
# SMTP is checked second, so a CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL takes precedence if both are
# present.

# SMTP — the default route. For Hostinger mailboxes:
#   SMTP_HOST=smtp.hostinger.com
#   SMTP_PORT=465            (implicit TLS; use 587 for STARTTLS)
#   SMTP_USER=contact@softauratechnology.com
#   SMTP_PASSWORD=<that mailbox's password>
# The password is a real credential: put it in .env.local and in your host's
# environment panel, never in this file and never in a commit.
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASSWORD=

# Alternative: POST the validated enquiry as JSON to a CRM, automation or your
# own endpoint. Takes precedence over SMTP when set.
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=
